{"id":"041b10825d75f464","group":"17","path":"17/17-df-definable-closure.md","title":"Definable Closure","display":"df-definable-closure — Definable Closure","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-df-definable-closure","aliases":["17-df-definable-closure"],"display":"df-definable-closure — Definable Closure","depends_on":["[[17-df-first-order-language]]","[[17-df-structure]]","[[17-df-parameter-definable-set]]"],"label_origin":"local-catalog","source_verification":"local supplementary closure operator; compared definable-element motivation only; exact book definition not located","source_verification_history":["not-compared-to-book-in-this-pass; local statement reviewed"],"source_section":"1.3; 3.1; 3.4","source_result":"Exercise 1.3.14*; named-parameter expansions; definable-element convention","source_pages_print":[35,137,185],"source_pages_djvu":[51,153,201],"verification_date":"2026-10-13","legacy_label":"17-df-1.6.3"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-df-definable-closure"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-df-definable-closure</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-definable-closure — Definable Closure"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"dab75c9f48db057d\" href=\"?note=dab75c9f48db057d\" title=\"17-df-first-order-language\">17-df-first-order-language</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" href=\"?note=fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" title=\"17-df-structure\">17-df-structure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"92c5e247a43bafd2\" href=\"?note=92c5e247a43bafd2\" title=\"17-df-parameter-definable-set\">17-df-parameter-definable-set</a></span></div>"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"local supplementary closure operator; compared definable-element motivation only; exact book definition not located"},{"key":"source_verification_history","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>not-compared-to-book-in-this-pass; local statement reviewed</span></div>"},{"key":"source_section","html":"1.3; 3.1; 3.4"},{"key":"source_result","html":"Exercise 1.3.14*; named-parameter expansions; definable-element convention"},{"key":"source_pages_print","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>35</span><span>137</span><span>185</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pages_djvu","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>51</span><span>153</span><span>201</span></div>"},{"key":"verification_date","html":"2026-10-13"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-df-1.6.3"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\\)</span>（语言，见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"dab75c9f48db057d\" href=\"?note=dab75c9f48db057d\" title=\"17-df-first-order-language\">17-df-first-order-language</a>）。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{A}\">\\(\\mathfrak{A}\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-structure, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" href=\"?note=fdac06af5a7f3bb5\" title=\"17-df-structure\">17-df-structure</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\\subseteq|\\mathfrak{A}|\">\\(X\\subseteq|\\mathfrak{A}|\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Def}_1(\\mathfrak{A};X)\">\\(\\operatorname{Def}_1(\\mathfrak{A};X)\\)</span> (unary sets definable with parameters from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"92c5e247a43bafd2\" href=\"?note=92c5e247a43bafd2\" title=\"17-df-parameter-definable-set\">17-df-parameter-definable-set</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{dcl}_{\\mathfrak{A}}\">\\(\\operatorname{dcl}_{\\mathfrak{A}}\\)</span> (operator defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{dcl}_{\\mathfrak{A}}(X)\n=\n\\{a\\in|\\mathfrak{A}|:\\{\\langle a\\rangle\\}\\in\\operatorname{Def}_1(\\mathfrak{A};X)\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\operatorname{dcl}_{\\mathfrak{A}}(X)\n=\n\\{a\\in|\\mathfrak{A}|:\\{\\langle a\\rangle\\}\\in\\operatorname{Def}_1(\\mathfrak{A};X)\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Def}_1\">\\(\\operatorname{Def}_1\\)</span> 的成员是载体的一元元组集，因此正式定义使用单点元组集 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\{\\langle a\\rangle\\}\">\\(\\{\\langle a\\rangle\\}\\)</span>。这与“用参数唯一地定义元素 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\">\\(a\\)</span>”等价，且避免把元素 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\">\\(a\\)</span> 与一元组 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\langle a\\rangle\">\\(\\langle a\\rangle\\)</span> 混同。</p>\n<p>来源边界：原书 Exercise 1.3.14*（p.35，DjVu51）与 §3.4（p.185，DjVu201）定义无参数的“唯一可定义元素”；§3.1（p.137，DjVu153）允许命名参数。本地 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{dcl}_{\\mathfrak A}\">\\(\\operatorname{dcl}_{\\mathfrak A}\\)</span> 将唯一可定义性应用于有限参数，是补充算子。全文 OCR 与定义索引未定位到 definable closure 的对应原书定义，故不声明原书已给出此闭包算子或其闭包定律。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-first-order-language","status":"resolved","id":"dab75c9f48db057d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","locati